    "passage": "Fred, a French exchange student, began to study at a middle school in Beijing to learn about Chinese culture last year.\nOne morning, excited to make a good impression, he gave his new roommate Wang Gang ___1___ warm hug—a common greeting in France. However, Wang felt uncomfortable.\nFred didn’t know the cultural difference and felt ___2___. Luckily, Fred’s classmate Zhao Rui told ___3___ hugs are usually for good friends or family in China.\nLater that day, Fred waved to his teacher Miss Chen with his palm up, ___4___ Miss Chen looked surprised. When Fred felt confused, Miss Chen explained, “It isn’t polite ___5___ others in this way in China. A handshake is much ___6___.”\nFeeling sorry ___7___ his mistakes, Fred held a small party for his teachers and classmates. He apologized for his improper body language. Then they talked ___8___, enjoyed delicious food while learning about each other’s customs.\nThrough this experience, Fred learned about Chinese ways of using body language and being ___9___. His classmates also ___10___ that being patient and open-minded is important when people have different customs. Their friendship and understanding finally brought them closer together.",
    "passageHtml": "<p><span class=\"ind\">Fred, a French exchange student, began to study at a middle school in Beijing to learn about Chinese culture last year.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">One morning, excited to make a good impression, he gave his new roommate Wang Gang <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;1&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> warm hug—a common greeting in France. However, Wang felt uncomfortable.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Fred didn’t know the cultural difference and felt <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;2&nbsp;&nbsp;</u>. Luckily, Fred’s classmate Zhao Rui told <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;3&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> hugs are usually for good friends or family in China.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Later that day, Fred waved to his teacher Miss Chen with his palm up, <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;4&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> Miss Chen looked surprised. When Fred felt confused, Miss Chen explained, “It isn’t polite <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;5&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> others in this way in China. A handshake is much <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;6&nbsp;&nbsp;</u>.”</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Feeling sorry <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;7&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> his mistakes, Fred held a small party for his teachers and classmates. He apologized for his improper body language. Then they talked <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;8&nbsp;&nbsp;</u>, enjoyed delicious food while learning about each other’s customs.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Through this experience, Fred learned about Chinese ways of using body language and being <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;9&nbsp;&nbsp;</u>. His classmates also <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;10&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> that being patient and open-minded is important when people have different customs. Their friendship and understanding finally brought them closer together.</span></p>",
    "intro": "本文讲述法国交换生Fred在北京因文化差异产生误解，最终通过沟通增进理解与友谊的故事。",
