    "title": "八下语法选择 · 二 皮划艇冒险与友谊",
    "passage": "Off the Map is a novel about adventure (冒险) and growing up. In the book, Amos and Marlo were best friends. From playing soccer to sitting together at lunch, they did everything together ___1___ Amos suddenly stopped talking to Marlo. Marlo found this very ___2___.\nMarlo was upset, but she didn’t want to shut ___3___ away. To forget her anger, she decided to go ___4___ a canoe (皮划艇) trip with her mother. But when they arrived, she saw clearly Amos and his father by the river. Their parents ___5___ them with a trip. Marlo thought it was ___6___ surprise ever.\nAfter their parents asked them to share a canoe, they started arguing. This made them take a wrong turn and get lost. They needed ___7___ together to find their way back to safety. They looked for solutions to face challenges, like bad weather and wild animals. During hard times, they talked about their friendship. Marlo learned ___8___ Amos behaved strangely, and Amos apologized to Marlo.\nThe novel is full of amazing adventures, but for the writer, the heart of the story is the conversations between Marlo and Amos. The writer wants readers to see how they cleared ___9___ air and rebuilt their trust. The writer also hopes readers enjoy ___10___ the outdoors and the meaning of friendship.",
    "passageHtml": "<p><span class=\"ind\"><i>Off the Map</i> is a novel about adventure (冒险) and growing up. In the book, Amos and Marlo were best friends. From playing soccer to sitting together at lunch, they did everything together <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;1&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> Amos suddenly stopped talking to Marlo. Marlo found this very <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;2&nbsp;&nbsp;</u>.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Marlo was upset, but she didn’t want to shut <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;3&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> away. To forget her anger, she decided to go <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;4&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> a canoe (皮划艇) trip with her mother. But when they arrived, she saw clearly Amos and his father by the river. Their parents <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;5&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> them with a trip. Marlo thought it was <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;6&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> surprise ever.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">After their parents asked them to share a canoe, they started arguing. This made them take a wrong turn and get lost. They needed <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;7&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> together to find their way back to safety. They looked for solutions to face challenges, like bad weather and wild animals. During hard times, they talked about their friendship. Marlo learned <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;8&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> Amos behaved strangely, and Amos apologized to Marlo.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">The novel is full of amazing adventures, but for the writer, the heart of the story is the conversations between Marlo and Amos. The writer wants readers to see how they cleared <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;9&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> air and rebuilt their trust. The writer also hopes readers enjoy <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;10&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> the outdoors and the meaning of friendship.</span></p>",
    "intro": "本文介绍冒险小说《Off the Map》，讲述Marlo和Amos因误会疏远，后在皮划艇旅行中面对挑战，最终消除误会重建友谊的故事。",
