    "passageHtml": "<p><span class=\"ind\">Once upon a time, there was a little boy. His parents were poor farmers. They couldn’t pay for a worker, <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;1&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> the boy had to help with the housework. He worked very hard.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Every day, he had a <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;2&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> rest at sunset (日落). But he didn’t choose to have a rest. Instead, he used that time to climb to <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;3&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> top of a hill. He saw the wonderful views of his hometown. Then a house on another hill <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;4&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> by him. It had golden windows. They were really bright like diamonds.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">One day, the boy’s father said to him, “You worked really hard, so you can have a rest today. Try to learn something good.” The boy thanked his father. Then, he left home and walked to the far hill <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;5&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> the house with golden windows.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">He came to the house and knocked <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;6&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> the door, and a girl answered. He told her about the golden windows. The girl shook <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;7&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> head and said, “Poor farmers like us only have glass windows. Look there! That’s the house with the golden windows. ” She <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;8&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> at something far away.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">When the boy looked, he was surprised to see his own house. He then thanked the girl and rushed home as <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;9&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> as possible.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Inside, he saw his family and smiled. He told them <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;10&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> he had an excellent day. He also said, “I learned a great lesson—our house has golden windows.” Then his family all laughed happily.</span></p>",
