    "passage": "We can do many interesting chemical tests in our class. Today, we will use CO2 to blow up a balloon! What\n※a balloon    ※a soft drink bottle    ※ some baking soda (苏打粉)    ※ some vinegar (醋)\nHow\nBefore you begin the test, make sure that you pull the balloon long to make it as easy as possible to blow it up. And put 40 ml of water into the soft drink bottle. Then follow the pictures to finish the test:\nWhy\nIf everything goes well, then the gas will make the balloon blow up. Introducing the vinegar (lemon juice is also OK) to the baking soda creates a chemical effect. The baking soda is a base (碱), while the vinegar is an acid (酸). When the two are mixed, they create CO2. The gas fills the soft drink bottle quickly. However, it doesn’t get away from the balloon, pushing it outwards and blowing it up.",
    "passageHtml": "<div style=\"overflow-x:auto;margin:10px 0\"><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;border:1px solid var(--bd);font-size:14px\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid var(--bd);padding:8px 12px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top;line-height:1.65\"><p style=\"margin:4px 0;text-align:left\">We can do many interesting chemical tests in our class. Today, we will use CO2 to blow up a balloon! <b>What</b></p><p style=\"margin:4px 0;text-align:left\">※a balloon    ※a soft drink bottle    ※ some baking soda (苏打粉)    ※ some vinegar (醋)</p><p style=\"margin:4px 0;text-align:left\"><b>How</b></p><p style=\"margin:4px 0;text-align:left\">Before you begin the test, make sure that you pull the balloon long to make it as easy as possible to blow it up. And put 40 ml of water into the soft drink bottle. Then follow the pictures to finish the test:</p><p style=\"margin:4px 0;text-align:left\"><div style=\"text-align:center;margin:6px 0\"><img src=\"assets/images/jr_read9a_19_1.png\" alt=\"插图\" style=\"width:291px;max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:4px\"></div><b>Why</b></p><p style=\"margin:4px 0;text-align:left\">If everything goes well, then the gas will make the balloon blow up. <u>Introducing</u> the vinegar (lemon juice is also OK) to the baking soda creates a chemical effect. The baking soda is a base (碱), while the vinegar is an acid (酸). When the two are mixed, they create CO2. The gas fills the soft drink bottle quickly. However, it doesn’t get away from the balloon, pushing it outwards and blowing it up.</p></td></tr></table></div>",
