    "title": "九上阅读 · 二十四 本周六下午将举办的免费制作“太阳",
    "passage": "Worried about mosquitoes (蚊子) and diseases like Dengue or Chikungunya fever?\nThis summer, let’s build a creative mosquito-repellent (防蚊) device to protect ourselves!\nMosquitoes are more than just annoying; they can carry diseases. In Guangdong, we need to be especially careful about viruses like Chikungunya. This makes it important to keep mosquitoes away. This weekend, join us to make a simple but creative “Solar-Powered Mosquito Repeller” FOR FREE. It’s a perfect way to learn about invention and stay healthy at the same time!\nTime: 2:30 p.m.—5:00 p.m., Saturday (August 16)\nPlace: Sunshine Community Center, Yuexiu District, Guangzhou\nPlease note:\nAll tools and materials (like small solar panels, safe electronic parts) will be provided as shown in the picture.\nFor 30 people only. The people must be 12 years old or above. First come, first served.\nTo book your place for the activity, please call Mr. Li at 020-87654321 by 8:00 p.m. this Friday.For those who want to try making it at home, here are the basic steps:\nConnect a small solar panel to a mini fan using safe wires.\nAttach a piece of mosquito-repellent paper to the front of the fan.\nCarefully make some small holes on the plastic bottle. Place the fan inside the bottle, facing the holes.\nPut the bottle where the sun can reach the solar panel. The sun powers the fan, which then blows the repellent smell out through the holes to keep mosquitoes away!",
