    "title": "九上阅读 · 三十 备考的几个实用方法",
    "passage": "Preparing for an exam can be stressful, but it doesn’t have to be. There’s no need to stress out or cram (突击准备). By doing a couple of simple things, you will be confident and ready for anything that comes up on the test.\n\n◆Start studying early.\n\nIf the class material is especially difficult for you, start studying early. Give yourself enough time to truly understand the material, practice it and then review it. Get a full night’s sleep before the exam. Your brain needs time to digest everything you’ve put into it, so start early and you don’t have to stay up all night.\n\n◆Read through your notes that may be on the exam.\n\nIt will refresh (刷新) your memory of the material and help you remember what you learnt. It will also help you to know all the information in your notes, including where it is located in your notes, so that you know where to find them, and what might be missing from your notes.\n\n◆Get some good notes.\n\nIf you’re not a good note taker, or there are “holes” in your notes, then ask a friend if you can copy his or her notes. Good notes can make all the difference when you’re studying. They make difficult points easier to understand and remember.\n\n◆Ask your teacher about the test material.\n\nOne of the easiest ways to begin your studying is to find out what is on the test directly from your teacher. Many teachers will provide some guidance on what will and will not be covered on the test. Knowing which material the test will cover can help you focus on the main material that you need to study.",
    "passageHtml": "<p><span class=\"ind\">Preparing for an exam can be stressful, but it doesn’t have to be. There’s no need to stress out or cram (突击准备). By doing a couple of simple things, you will be confident and ready for anything that comes up on the test.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">◆Start studying early.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">If the class material is especially difficult for you, start studying early. Give yourself enough time to truly understand the material, practice it and then review it. Get a full night’s sleep before the exam. Your brain needs time to <u>digest</u> everything you’ve put into it, so start early and you don’t have to stay up all night.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">◆Read through your notes that may be on the exam.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">It will refresh (刷新) your memory of the material and help you remember what you learnt. It will also help you to know all the information in your notes, including where it is located in your notes, so that you know where to find them, and what might be missing from your notes.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">◆Get some good notes.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">If you’re not a good note taker, or there are “holes” in your notes, then ask a friend if you can copy his or her notes. Good notes can make all the difference when you’re studying. They make difficult points easier to understand and remember.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">◆Ask your teacher about the test material.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">One of the easiest ways to begin your studying is to find out what is on the test directly from your teacher. Many teachers will provide some guidance on what will and will not be covered on the test. Knowing which material the test will cover can help you focus on the main material that you need to study.</span></p>",
    "intro": "本文是一篇说明文，主要讲述了备考的几个实用方法，包括提前开始学习、通读笔记、补充完善笔记、向老师咨询考试范围等。",
