    "title": "九上阅读 · 三十八 第15届中国国际航空航天博览会",
    "passage": "The 15th China International Aviation and Aerospace Expo—Zhuhai Airshow\n\nZhuhai, a lively city located in Guangdong Province, is well-known for its biennial(两年一度的) airshow, which draws visitors from around the world. This year, the airshow will take place from November 12 to 17, 2024.\n\nViewing venues\n\nTo further enrich the display content and meet the different viewing needs of the audience, this year’s China Airshow has opened three viewing venues. They are the Zhuhai International Aerospace Center, the Jin Feng Tai viewing area, and the China Airshow Unmanned Aircraft and Unmanned Ship Demonstration Area (Doumen Lianzou).\n\nPrices of the tickets to the Zhuhai International Aerospace Center:\n\nIndividual Ticket: ¥500.\n\nDiscount Ticket: ¥350 (the people aged 60 and above (born before November 15, 1964) and under 18 years old (born after November 15, 2006).\n\nAirshow Package Tickets: from ¥650 to ¥1999\n\nOfficial Ticket Sales Channels of China Airshow:\n\nThere are four ways to get the tickets, including the Official Website www.airshow.com.cn, Official WeChat Public Account “China Airshow”, “Zhuhai Airshow” WeChat Mini Program or “Zhuhai Airshow” App.\n\nMore things should be paid attention:\n\nFor one thing, this year’s airshow tickets are real-name ID-type tickets and cannot be transferred to others for use. Otherwise, entry to the exhibition will be refused .Besides, tickets will not be sold at the airshow entrance. If you want to enjoy the show, remember to buy tickets in advance (提前).\n\nFor more information, you can call the Ticket Consultation Hotline, 400-8800-113.",
    "passageHtml": "<p class=\"ct\">The 15th China International Aviation and Aerospace Expo—Zhuhai Airshow</p><p><span class=\"ind\">Zhuhai, a lively city located in Guangdong Province, is well-known for its biennial(两年一度的) airshow, which draws visitors from around the world. This year, the airshow will take place from November 12 to 17, 2024.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Viewing venues</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">To further enrich the display content and meet the different viewing needs of the audience, this year’s China Airshow has opened three viewing venues. They are the Zhuhai International Aerospace Center, the Jin Feng Tai viewing area, and the China Airshow Unmanned Aircraft and Unmanned Ship Demonstration Area (Doumen Lianzou).</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Prices of the tickets to the Zhuhai International Aerospace Center:</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Individual Ticket: ¥500.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Discount Ticket: ¥350 (the people aged 60 and above (born before November 15, 1964) and under 18 years old (born after November 15, 2006).</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Airshow Package Tickets: from ¥650 to ¥1999</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Official Ticket Sales Channels of China Airshow:</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">There are four ways to get the tickets, including the Official Website www.airshow.com.cn, Official WeChat Public Account “China Airshow”, “Zhuhai Airshow” WeChat Mini Program or “Zhuhai Airshow” App.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">More things should be paid attention:</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">For one thing, this year’s airshow tickets are real-name ID-type tickets and cannot be transferred to others for use. Otherwise, entry to the exhibition will be refused .Besides, tickets will not be sold at the airshow entrance. If you want to enjoy the show, remember to buy tickets in advance (提前).</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">For more information, you can call the Ticket Consultation Hotline, 400-8800-113.</span></p>",
    "intro": "本文介绍了第15届中国国际航空航天博览会，也称珠海航展的信息，包括其举办时间、观赏场地、门票价格及购买渠道等注意事项。",
